# Misty Salon counts the unlocked doors among Rooms "you control" (CR 709.5c, 109.5): an opponent's Room is not one. On turn 2
# Bot2 casts Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon as Smoky Lounge with Black Lotus's {R}{R}{R}, a Room with one unlocked door. On turn 3
# Bot1 casts its own copy as Misty Salon ({3}{U}) with Black Lotus's {U}{U}{U} and Mox Sapphire: the trigger counts only its
# own unlocked door, so a 1/1 blue flying Spirit, not a 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon.Cast(Ability: Smoky Lounge)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Smoky Lounge.Doors = Smoky Lounge
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon.Cast(Ability: Misty Salon)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

